        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "714bd422-6ec6-5db3-8eb7-e46ab28cda0f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Royle Family; Half the World Away; All My Demons Greeting Me as a Friend; Brookside; Waking the Dead; Coronation Street; Downton Abbey\n- People: Sue Johnston; Ricky Tomlinson; Caroline Aherne; Ralf Little; Craig Cash\n- Organizations: BBC; ITV Studios; Channel 4; ITV\n- Places: Manchester\n\nFacts:\n- The Royle Family is a British television sitcom produced by ITV Studios for the BBC that ran for three series from 1998 to 2000 and returned with specials from 2006 to 2012.\n- The Royle Family centres on the lives of a scruffy, television-fixated family in Manchester called the Royles.\n- The Royle Family features Jim Royle played by Ricky Tomlinson, Barbara Royle played by Sue Johnston, Denise played by Caroline Aherne, Antony played by Ralf Little, and Denise’s fiancé and later husband David played by Craig Cash.\n- Sue Johnston, born Susan Wright on 7 December 1943, is an English actress.\n- Sue Johnston played Sheila Grant in the Channel 4 soap opera Brookside from 1982 to 1990.\n- Sue Johnston played Barbara Royle in the BBC comedy The Royle Family from 1998 to 2012.\n- Sue Johnston played Grace Foley in the BBC drama Waking the Dead from 2000 to 2011.\n- Sue Johnston played Gloria Price in the ITV soap opera Coronation Street from 2012 to 2014.\n- Sue Johnston played Miss Denker in the ITV drama Downton Abbey from 2014 to 2015.\n- Half the World Away is well known as the theme tune to the BBC sitcom The Royle Family.\n- All My Demons Greeting Me as a Friend includes the singles Runaway, Running With The Wolves, Murder Song (5, 4, 3, 2, 1), Half the World Away, Conqueror, I Went Too Far, and Winter Bird.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "98bab6e5-fb6f-5fbe-97ca-ebbb645f394f",
        "text": "Page: The Royle Family. Sentence: The Royle Family is a British television sitcom produced by ITV Studios for the BBC, which ran for three series from 1998-2000, and specials from 2006-12.\nPage: The Royle Family. Sentence: It centres on the lives of a scruffy television-fixated Manchester family, the Royles, comprising family patriarch Jim Royle (Ricky Tomlinson), his wife Barbara (Sue Johnston), their daughter Denise (Caroline Aherne), their son Antony (Ralf Little) and Denise's fiancé (later husband) David (Craig Cash).\nPage: Sue Johnston. Sentence: Sue Johnston OBE (born Susan Wright; born 7 December 1943) is an English actress known for playing Sheila Grant in the Channel 4 soap opera \"Brookside\" (1982–1990), Barbara Royle in the BBC comedy \"The Royle Family\" (1998–2012), Grace Foley in the BBC drama \"Waking the Dead\" (2000–2011), Gloria Price in the ITV soap opera \"Coronation Street\" (2012–2014) and Miss Denker in the ITV drama \"Downton Abbey\" (2014–2015).\nPage: Half the World Away. Sentence: It is well known as the theme tune to the popular BBC sitcom \"The Royle Family\".\nPage: All My Demons Greeting Me as a Friend. Sentence: The album includes singles \"Runaway\", \"Running With The Wolves\", \"Murder Song (5, 4, 3, 2, 1)\", \"Half the World Away\", \"Conqueror\", \"I Went Too Far\", and \"Winter Bird\".",
